# Learning Styles and Student Performance in Introductory Economics

**Authors:** Brunton, Bruce

## Abstract
Data from nine introductory microeconomics classes was used to test the effect of student learning style on academic performance. The Kolb Learning Style Inventory was used to assess individual student learning styles. The results indicate that student learning style has no significant effect on performance, undermining the claims of those who advocate greater instructional design concern for different learning styles.

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ1049571

